<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Tradeoff: App Sandbox is deliberately left OFF (no `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` key).

	  HotkeyManager (Phase 2) needs a global NSEvent monitor for the hold-to-talk gesture
	  (Ctrl+Option+Space keyDown/keyUp), which requires Accessibility permission and does not
	  reliably deliver events outside the app's own windows when the app is sandboxed. A fully
	  sandboxed build would need a separate Accessibility-permission XPC helper to keep the
	  global monitor working, which is out of scope for v1.

	  Because the app is non-sandboxed, no `com.apple.security.device.audio-input` entitlement
	  is required either: microphone access is governed purely by the
	  NSMicrophoneUsageDescription Info.plist key and the standard macOS TCC consent prompt.

	  Cost: this app cannot be distributed via the Mac App Store as-is (sandboxing is mandatory
	  there). Acceptable for an indie/direct-distributed menu-bar utility for now — revisit if
	  App Store distribution becomes a goal (tracked in backlog.md).
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
